29883d4ec35a31a8393c4ffb220888c44c0bb022:tools/round-44/carriers.json:1037:  "note": "Frozen carriers for R44-C1: squashfs_v1 + squashfs_v2 (both byte orders) through REA 6.5.0 extract-firmware -> Core. Bytes are the committed MIT unblob 26.6.4 fixtures (tools/round-42/fixtures.json); they were round-42 C2 held-out INPUTS, never a C1 carrier. The oracle is independent: /usr/bin/unsquashfs (squashfs-tools 4.7.5) -lls member census + extracted member digests, plus the unblob __output__ expected tree (S138, second oracle). v2ns stays Frontier (no independent reader).",
29883d4ec35a31a8393c4ffb220888c44c0bb022:tools/round-44/carriers.json:1062:    "exploratory_note": "the squashfs_v2 2.1 pair: measured and retained, but UNBOUND exploratory data, NOT scored (its REA probe was exploratory and unretained, so the C1 target was reverted to the four preregistered carriers)",
29883d4ec35a31a8393c4ffb220888c44c0bb022:tools/round-44/carriers.json:1076:    "compression": "ABSENT - the v1/v2 superblock has no compression field; the compression class is observed from the inode-table metadata block (zlib header 78xx => gzip)",
29883d4ec35a31a8393c4ffb220888c44c0bb022:tools/round-44/carriers.json:1081:    "file_caveat": "file(1) applies the squashfs v4 layout to every squashfs image, so its compressed/uncompressed word for a v1/v2 image is read from offset 20 (inode_table_start), NOT from a compression field; it must not be bound by the counter",
29883d4ec35a31a8393c4ffb220888c44c0bb022:tools/round-44/carriers.json:1098:    "note": "SquashFS v1/v2 superblock is 32 bytes (packed), per unblob 26.6.4 SquashFSv1Handler.C_DEFINITIONS (S119). THE v1/v2 SUPERBLOCK HAS NO COMPRESSION FIELD.",
